# 43. Cybersecurity Connection

Linux permissions are directly related to cybersecurity.

Incorrect permissions can expose:

```text
Passwords
SSH keys
Configuration files
Application data
Logs
Private documents
Database credentials
Scripts
System files
```

For example:

```text
Incorrect permissions
        ↓
Unauthorized access
        ↓
Sensitive information exposed
        ↓
Potential security incident
```

Therefore, understanding Linux permissions is an important foundation for:

```text
Cybersecurity
System Administration
Digital Forensics
Penetration Testing
SOC Analysis
Incident Response
Cloud Security
DevSecOps
```

