# 44. Final Takeaway

Linux permissions are not just commands to memorize.

The important idea is:

```text
WHO
 ↓
CAN DO WHAT
 ↓
TO WHICH RESOURCE?
```

For example:

```text
User
 ↓
Can read
 ↓
secret.txt
```

or:

```text
Web service
 ↓
Can read
 ↓
website files
```

Good permission management reduces unauthorized access and follows the principle of least privilege.

My goal is to understand **why a permission exists, what it allows, what happens when it is removed, and how incorrect permissions can create security risks**.
